  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking Changes\n\t\t\t----------------\n\t\t\t- Enum Updates:\n\t\t\t\t- DriverStatus, CountryCode, and ShardType enums modified.\n\t\t\t- Removed underscores from values.\n\t\t\t- Applied proper casing (e.g., Na, Eu, etc.).\n\t\t\t- Method Renames Casing Adjustments:\n\t\t\t\t- AuthenticateWithSSID renamed to AuthenticateWithSsid.\n\t\t\t- All instances of ssid, clid, csid, tlid are now properly cased (SSID → Ssid).\n\t\t\t- Cancellation tokens added to:\n\t\t\t\t- SpikeHandler, KillFeedHandler\n\t\t\t- Removed obsolete methods (warnings present for ~5 versions):\n\t\t\t- PerformDriverCacheRequest\n\t\t\t- ValorantNet(string ssid)\n\t\t\t- GetPeakValorantRankAsync (PRs welcome to re-add).\n\t\t\t- Case changes to various record properties (names remain the same).\n\t\t\t- GetValorantPath and GetRiotClientPath now return empty on non-Windows builds.\n\t\t\t- ValorantNet now errors if Access Token or Entitlement Token cannot be built.\n\n\t\t\tMethod Expandability\n\t\t\t--------------------\n\t\t\t- StringExtensions is now internal (no longer visible externally).\n\t\t\t- InternalValorantMethods.ClientIsReady (bool) is now public\n\t\t\t(not sensitive, potentially useful for some users).",
  "repository": "",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "Radiant Connect Valorant API (UnOfficial)",
